{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:8.55.060","page_type":"section"},"citation":"8.55.060","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/8.55.060","content_hash":"8e50bd82b580d0303207b016de711e3db42605a4ccbcefcd9dfae11e1d82abd8","heading":"Fee assessment.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.55.060:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/8.55.060","text":"(a) Any person using an alarm system that reports, or causes to report, false alarms shall be assessed a fee based on the number of responses to false fire alarms within a calendar year. Calendar year shall be from January 1st to December 31st. Fees for false alarm responses shall be prescribed by the City’s fee schedule and based on the number of previous occurrences as follows:\nFALSE ALARM RESPONSES\n0 – 3\n4 – 10\n11 – 20\n21 – 30\n31 – 50\n51 or more\nFALSE ALARM RESPONSES\n0 – 3\n4 – 10\n11 – 20\n21 – 30\n31 – 50\n51 or more\n(b) An invoice assessing a false alarm fee will be delivered to the alarm user by regular mail or by email and the fee is due within 30 days of the date of the invoice assessing the fee.\n(c) Any person who receives an invoice imposing a fee, charge or penalty may, within 10 business days from the date of the invoice, appeal all or part of the fee, charge or penalty in accordance with TMC 2.45.020 . (Ord. 20631 § 40, 1-13-26.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"d046fe53-df40-5b36-9795-34b765962aa2"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"8.55.060","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/8.55.060","content_hash":"15da36bb18011ef4258e625a24298c882cbe49be9f609fcaf6710ed7f8159434","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.55.